  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Nebraska total $1B for FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 19.0% year over year. The state recorded 15,203 awards with an average award size of $67.5K. The Department of Defense obligated $371M, the Department of Education obligated $287M, and the General Services Administration obligated $171M so far this fiscal year. NELNET SERVICING LLC received $287M, making Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation the largest industry by dollars at $287M. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $200M and Engineering Services accounted for $98.7M. Historical totals show obligations at $1.3B in FY21, $1.3B in FY22, $2B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, $1.3B in FY25, and $1B in FY26. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). This snapshot highlights where federal money is concentrated by agency, vendor, and NAICS industry in Nebraska for the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the year-over-year decline in obligations?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 19.0% year over year. The Department of Defense remains the largest buyer with $371M, but the total for FY2026 to date is $1B compared with prior-year fiscal totals such as $1.3B in FY25 and $2B in FY23. Large single vendors and industries concentrated dollars: NELNET SERVICING LLC received $287M and Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation accounted for $287M, which can shift totals when large awards arise or do not repeat."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate Nebraska contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense, the Department of Education, and the General Services Administration are the top buyers with $371M, $287M, and $171M respectively. NELNET SERVICING LLC, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC., and HENDRICKSON TRANSPORTATION LLC lead vendors with $287M, $154M, and $43.7M respectively. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation, Computer Systems Design Services, and Engineering Services lead industries with $287M, $200M, and $98.7M respectively."
      }
    ]
